37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"It seems my suspicions were correct. The car is often left in a poor state, and the most consistent weekly trips are the ones being disrupted. We need to address the basic etiquette of handovers.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"Oh, the drama! It turns out that trying to be ""precise"" with our figures actually made us all hate each other. Who knew that checking the math could be so toxic? We're spending way too much energy on this.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a reminder that numbers alone cannot capture the spirit of sharing. While the fixed costs are substantial, the diary shows our needs fluctuate greatly. We must balance the cold math with a warm heart.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@May, exactly. Checking figures just makes us feel accused. Other groups said the same thing—asking for favors or clinging to turns is what actually ruins things. We're focusing on the wrong stuff.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@May, @Takumi, I see your point, but look! The fuel receipts show it's really lopsided. Some of us are paying way more than others. We can't just ignore that if we want to be fair!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, money is important, but it doesn't matter who pays if the car is empty or dirty when you need it. We can't just balance the books; we need a standard for how the car is returned.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, you're so right! But @Kenji, if we spend all our time arguing over pennies and scrubbing seats, we're just wasting our lives. Maybe the ""fair"" way is the one that takes the least effort?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, simplicity is indeed a form of wisdom. However, we must ensure that ""least effort"" does not become a burden for one person while others enjoy the ease. True peace comes from a balance that satisfies the soul and the wallet.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, that's why we can't just use a spreadsheet to solve this. If we keep treating each other like accountants, we're just going to keep fighting. We need a system where we don't have to beg for favors.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I'm not trying to be an accountant, but it's not just ""pennies""! Some people are paying for almost everything while others pay almost nothing. That's not fair to our friends, right? We need a real plan for the money!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, fairness isn't just about the money. It's also about the reliability of the car. If the weekly trips keep collapsing, the system is failing regardless of who paid for the fuel. We need a rule for handovers.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I'm with you on the reliability, but let's be real: the ""rules"" are exactly what's killing us. We're spending more time managing the car than actually driving it! Why not just simplify everything?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@May, simplicity is a beacon, but we must not let it blind us to the truth. If we ignore the costs, we risk a quiet resentment that will erode our friendship more surely than any rulebook.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, resentment comes from feeling controlled or accused, not just from money. If we make a rigid rulebook to ""save"" the friendship, we'll just find something new to fight about. We need to stop the policing.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I'm not talking about policing! I'm talking about helping each other. If some of us are paying way more, the others should help out. That's what friends do, right? We just need a simple way to share the cost!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, helping each other means ensuring the car is ready for the next person. If we only fix the payments but ignore the rubbish and empty tanks, we're still failing each other. We need a basic standard of care.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I love the spirit, but let's not create a chore list that feels like a second job! If we make it too rigid, we'll just be back to arguing over who missed a spot. Let's find a way to be chill about it!","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@May, @Misaki, you both speak a truth. We must care for the vehicle and our peace of mind. Let us seek a path where responsibility is a gesture of kindness, not a heavy chain of obligation.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, that sounds nice, but ""gestures of kindness"" don't stop the fighting when someone's being selfish. We need a system that stops us from having to ask for favors or police each other. Let's just keep it simple.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I agree we should keep it simple! But simple doesn't mean ignoring the facts. If we just ""be chill"" while some people pay for everything, that's not simple, it's just unfair. Let's find a way to be fair without being boring!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
