62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A seems the most reliable. If we have fixed days, the weekly trips won't collapse, and it's clear who is responsible for the car's state at the end of their turn.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A is a dream! No more endless coordinating or ""who owes what"" drama every single night. We just know it's our day and we're done with the paperwork. It's so much more chill!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"While Option A offers a serene simplicity, we must consider if a fixed share truly reflects the uneven usage we discovered. Is it fair to pay the same for a Tuesday as for a Saturday?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, that's exactly the kind of thinking that leads to the ""checking figures"" disaster. If we obsess over who uses it more, we'll just start policing each other again. Option A stops the favors and the fighting.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I see why you like A, but @Servas is right! If some people barely use the car but pay the same as those who drive it every day, that's not fair. Option C lets us pay for what we actually use!","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, Option C requires the very recording and policing that @Takumi and @May are worried about. If we want to stop the fighting, we need a system that doesn't require constant auditing of every single kilometer.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Takumi"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, exactly! Option C is just a fancy way of saying ""let's go back to being accountants."" I can't imagine spending my evenings calculating distances. Let's just pick A and reclaim our free time!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, your desire for freedom is understandable. Yet, we must ask: does a fixed share create a hidden burden? If one person quietly subsidizes another, the peace we find today may be but a mask for tomorrow's resentment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, you're doing it again. You're worrying about a ""hidden burden"" that hasn't happened yet, while the actual fighting is happening right now. Option A is the only one that stops us from acting like enemies.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, but the fighting is happening because the money is a mess! If we just ignore it with Option A, the people paying more will still feel it. Option B might be a better middle ground? One person manages it, and we just pay per trip!","{""words"":46,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Kenji, Option B puts too much pressure on one person and doesn't solve the reliability issue. If the Primary Keeper is busy, we're back to begging for favors. Option A ensures the car is available.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Misaki, you've hit the nail on the head! Option B just creates a ""boss"" of the car, and that sounds like a recipe for more tension. Let's just go with A and stop overthinking it!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is true that we must avoid the trap of overthinking. However, let us remember that true harmony is not the absence of conflict, but the presence of justice. I shall vote for the path of most balance.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, ""justice"" is just another word for the policing that's killing our friendship. We need to stop treating this like a court case. Option A is the only way to stop the favors and the fighting. I'm voting A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I'm not trying to make this a court case! I just want us to be honest. But if everyone hates the paperwork of Option C, maybe A is the only way we'll actually stop fighting. I'll think about it!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"Option A is the only choice that guarantees the car is where it should be on a midweek morning. It replaces constant negotiation with a simple, reliable routine. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for Option A too! Let's stop the endless chatting and the math headaches. I'm choosing my sanity and my free evenings over a spreadsheet any day. Option A is the winner in my book!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"I have listened to you all with an open heart. While I worry about the hidden costs of a fixed share, the peace of our friendship is the greatest treasure. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I've said it already. We need to stop the policing and the begging for favors before we completely fall apart. I'm voting for Option A. Let's just be friends again.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I really wanted the money to be perfect, but I don't want to be the only one fighting for it while everyone else is miserable. If it keeps us friends, I'm in! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
